Keep a shared strings as an empty list of text.
Place "0.1(6)" into strings.
Place "0.1666(6)" into strings.
Keep a shared text as empty text.
Keep a shared digits as 0.
Keep a shared power as 0.
Keep a shared foundpos as 0.
Keep a shared upper as 0.
Keep a shared lower as 0.
Keep a shared firsttop as 0.
Keep a shared firstbottom as 0.
Keep a shared secondtop as 0.
Keep a shared secondbottom as 0.
To finddot.
Set foundpos to -1.
For every spot from 0 to the last position of text.
If character spot of text is ".", set foundpos to spot, return.

To findopen.
Set foundpos to -1.
For every spot from 0 to the last position of text.
If character spot of text is "(", set foundpos to spot, return.

To findclose.
Set foundpos to -1.
For every spot from 0 to the last position of text.
If character spot of text is ")", set foundpos to spot, return.

To valueof from start (a whole number) with finish (a whole number).
Set digits to 0.
For every spot from start to finish minus 1.
The digit is the digit value of character spot of text.
Set digits to digits times 10 plus digit.

To raiseten with count (a whole number).
Set power to 1.
Repeat while count is more than 0.
Set power to power times 10.
Subtract 1 from count.

To parse.
Finddot.
The dot is foundpos.
Findopen.
The open is foundpos.
The last is the last position of text.
The length is last plus 1.
The whole is 0.
Valueof from 0 with dot.
Set whole to digits.
The fractionend is open.
If open is less than 0, set fractionend to length.
The fractionstart is dot plus 1.
Valueof from fractionstart with fractionend.
The fractionpart is digits.
The fractionlength is fractionend minus fractionstart.
The repeating is 0.
The repeatinglength is 0.
If open is at least 0.
Findclose.
The close is foundpos.
Valueof from open plus 1 with close.
Set repeating to digits.
Set repeatinglength to close minus open minus 1.
Raiseten with repeatinglength.
The repeatingscale is power.
The unit is repeatingscale minus 1.
Raiseten with fractionlength.
The fractionscale is power.
The denominator is fractionscale times unit.
The numerator is fractionpart times unit plus repeating.
Set upper to whole times denominator plus numerator.
Set lower to denominator.

For every spot from 0 to 1.
Set text to item spot of strings.
Parse.
If spot is 0, set firsttop to upper, set firstbottom to lower.
If spot is 1, set secondtop to upper, set secondbottom to lower.

The left is firsttop times secondbottom.
The right is secondtop times firstbottom.
If left is right, show true, otherwise show false.
